;; si's natives, the package arbace/scminterp (doc/scheme/SCHEME-SURVEY.md, SC61 (a), SC240; "As built: the embedding's gaps"):
;; the Go side of arbace.lang.SchemeInterp, whose natives j2g translates into calls of scminterp's SchemeInterp_<name>_native (as
;; arbace.lang.CInterp's are cinterp's, doc/C23-SURVEY.md, CS103). It imports arbace/scm and jrt; scm imports std only, so the light
;; path (test/scheme/si-driver) builds it without jrt. Write-ahead: built and checked in the re-seed window (j2g's rule for
;; SchemeInterp and the copy of scm and scminterp into the program); bin/si interp-check builds it with a stand-in jrt.
(ns go.arbace.scminterp
  (:require [arbace.go :as go]))

(go/package scminterp
  :path "arbace/scminterp"
  :files ["natives.go"])

(load "scminterp/natives")
